-- title:
--   Semilinear Galois action on the relative Picard model of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $p$ is a prime, $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and $L$ a field of characteristic zero which is a $p$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, equipped with an element $\zeta$ that is a primitive $p$-th root of unity. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ subject to `hK`, which identifies it with [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational function field of $X_1(Mp)$. The ring $A$ is a discrete valuation domain with an algebra structure over which $L$ is its fraction field; `hAp` places $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and `hζA` requires $\zeta$ to lie in the image of $A$ in $L$. Further, $A$ acts on $K$ compatibly with $L$ (scalar tower), and $j \in K$ is the element whose Laurent expansion is, by `hj`, the coefficientwise image [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, and is nonzero.
--
--   The integral model is the two-chart model morphism $X =$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, assumed proper, together with: a section $\varepsilon$, i.e. a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \to X$ splitting the structure morphism; a relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ designation $D$, that is a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and a zero section; and the hypothesis `hrep`, asserting that $D$ represents, in the sense of `RepresentsRelSubPic`, the subfunctor of the $\varepsilon$-rigidified relative Picard functor of $X/A$ cut out by `algEquivZeroCut` (fibrewise algebraic equivalence to zero of the rigidified line bundle on all geometric fibres), the data consisting of a Poincaré bundle lying in the cut, the universal property that every rigidified bundle in the cut is classified by a unique morphism over the base, and the triviality of the Poincaré bundle pulled back along the zero section. Regularity hypotheses: $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is smooth (`hsm`) and separated (`hsep`); the base change of $X$ to $L$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$ (`hsmL`) and geometrically integral (`hgiL`); and the second projection $D.P \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} L \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ is proper (`hprL`) and geometrically connected (`hgcL`). Algebra structures on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` over $A$ and over $L$, forming a scalar tower, are fixed.
--
--   The geometric fibre is presented by a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182), i.e. an integral scheme $M_\eta.C$, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with a ring isomorphism of that field with the function field of $M_\eta.C$ compatible with the base field, and a bijection between closed points and places. It is compared with $X$ by an isomorphism $e_\eta : M_\eta.C \to X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `heη` saying that $e_\eta$ followed by the second projection is $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$. Three compatibility hypotheses pin the comparison: the open subscheme of $M_\eta.C$ obtained as the preimage, under $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection, of the image of the finite chart immersion [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.ιFin`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L231) is nonempty; `hMηpin` says that for every $a$ in the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135) the element of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` obtained by transporting, via $M_\eta.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, the germ at the generic point of the pullback of $a$ to that open has Laurent expansion equal to the coefficientwise image under $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the Laurent expansion of $a$; and `hgal` says that for every $g \in \operatorname{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ fixing the image of $L$ pointwise and all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M_\eta.C$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, if $x'$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec} g$ followed by the same composite applied to $x$, then the place attached to $x'$ by `Mη.pointEquivPlace` is the image of the place attached to $x$ under the action of [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)) g`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54), the semilinear automorphism of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` induced by $g$ on Laurent coefficients.
--
--   Two further inputs at level $Mp$ are assumed: `hin`, the predicate [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsAll (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L58) (Hecke input data at every prime together with, for every $d$ coprime to $Mp$, a diamond automorphism of the rational function field and a base-changed automorphism of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`), and `hcomm`, the predicate [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondCommuteBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L54) asserting that all the generators `heckeDiamondGenBar (M * p)` commute pairwise. The Galois group $\operatorname{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$, realised as $L \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} L$, acts on $A$ by ring and semiring automorphisms, and `hΓA` requires $\operatorname{algebraMap}_{A \to L}(s \cdot a) = s(\operatorname{algebraMap}_{A \to L}(a))$ for all $s$ and $a$.
--
--   The points dictionary consists of a bijection `gpts` between [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of degree-zero divisors modulo principal divisors on `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`, and the set of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ (morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to D.P$ whose composite with $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is `specMap A (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`), together with `hgadd`, which says that `gpts` carries addition to the relative group law `RepresentsRelSubPic.relativeGroupLaw` attached to the chosen representability datum through the group cut `algEquivZeroGroupCut`.
--
--   The Abel–Jacobi data, over $L$ and over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, are: `hDL`, a representability datum for the base change of $X$ to $L$ with section `sectionBaseChange L ε` and designation `D.baseChange L`; a morphism $\mathrm{aj}_L$ from the base change of $X$ to $L$ to $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L).\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} L$; a morphism $k_L$ between the two pullbacks of $X$ along $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ and $\operatorname{Spec} L \to \operatorname{Spec} A$; a morphism $\overline{\mathrm{aj}} : M_\eta.C \to D.P$; and a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\bar\varepsilon$ of $M_\eta.C$. These are constrained by: `hPL`, an isomorphism between the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` and the one obtained by `BaseChange.ofR` from the pullback of the chosen Poincaré bundle along the first projection of $D.P \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A}\operatorname{Spec} L$; `hajLε`, that the base-changed section followed by $\mathrm{aj}_L$ is the zero section of $D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L$; `hajL`, that for every field $K'$, every morphism $t : \operatorname{Spec} K' \to \operatorname{Spec} L$ and every $K'$-point $x$ of $X_L$ over $t$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of `hDL` along $x$ followed by $\mathrm{aj}_L$ is isomorphic to the tensor product of the line bundle (dual of the ideal sheaf module) of the relative effective Cartier divisor of the point $x$ with the ideal sheaf module of the relative effective Cartier divisor of the point $t$ followed by the base-changed section, so that $\mathrm{aj}_L$ classifies the class of $[x] - [\varepsilon]$; `hkL₁` and `hkL₂`, which say that $k_L$ composed with the first projection over $L$ is the first projection over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and composed with the second projection over $L$ is the second projection over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} L$; `hajbar`, that $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ is $e_\eta$ followed by $k_L$, by $\mathrm{aj}_L$ and by the first projection of $D.P \times_{\operatorname{Spec} A} \operatorname{Spec} L$; `hajbar_over`, that $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ followed by $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ equals $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$; `hεbar`, that $\bar\varepsilon$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ followed by $\varepsilon$; `hεbar_aj`, that $\bar\varepsilon$ followed by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ followed by the zero section of $D$; and `hpts_aj`, that for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $M_\eta.C$ such that $s$ is the cusp section in the sense of `hεbar`, there exists a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ on `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` equal to $[\,$place of $x\,] - [\,$place of $s\,]$ as a finitely supported function on places, whose class satisfies $\mathrm{gpts}(\mathrm{Pic}^0\text{-class of } D_v) = x$ followed by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the assertion is: there exists a family $\tau$ assigning to each $s \in L \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} L$ a morphism $\tau_s : D.P \to D.P$ satisfying $\tau_s$ followed by $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ $=$ $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ followed by the morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ induced by the ring automorphism $a \mapsto s \cdot a$, such that for every $\sigma' \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every $s \in L \simeq_{\mathbb{Q}} L$ with $\sigma'(\operatorname{algebraMap}_{L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}} l) = \operatorname{algebraMap}_{L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}}(s\, l)$ for all $l \in L$, and for every $x \in$ [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186),
--   $$\mathrm{gpts}(\sigma' \cdot x) \;=\; \operatorname{Spec}(\sigma') \text{ followed by } \mathrm{gpts}(x) \text{ followed by } \tau_{s^{-1}} .$$
--   No multiplicativity in $s$, and no uniqueness of $\tau$, is asserted.
--
--   This is the Galois half of the operator layer on the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the stable two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$: the action of $\operatorname{Gal}(\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)/\mathbb{Q})$ on the base is lifted to a family of semilinear model self-maps of the Picard scheme which, read through the Abel–Jacobi dictionary on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points, implements the Galois action on $J_1(Mp)(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$. It feeds [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_heckeHom_galoisHom_pts_smul_eq_comp_abelJacobi_of_representsRelSubPic_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_heckeHom_galoisHom_pts_smul_eq_comp_abelJacobi_of_representsRelSubPic_twoChartModel_x1_mul), where it is combined with the Hecke and diamond operators on the same model.
